flowchart TB
  accTitle: A · Initial compiler lifecycle
  accDescr: Successful initial compile flow. Plugin cache loading and writing are conditional. B is module graph construction and C is resource generation. Observation seal is a Core operation, not a plugin hook. Update is independent.
  Begin([Compiler::new]) --> config[config]:::serial
  config --> Compile([Compiler::compile]) --> Cache{Persistent cache enabled<br/>and this plugin has a record?}:::gate
  Cache -->|yes| plugin_cache_loaded[plugin_cache_loaded]:::serial
  Cache -->|no| build_start[build_start]:::parallel
  plugin_cache_loaded --> build_start
  build_start --> B["B · Build module graph<br/>expanded below"]:::core
  B --> C["C · Generate resources<br/>expanded below"]:::core --> finish[finish]:::parallel
  finish --> Seal["Core: seal source observations<br/>reject changed / inconsistent inputs"]:::core
  Seal -->|accepted| Write{Persistent cache enabled?}:::gate
  Seal -. rejected .-> Error([Compilation error]):::core
  Write -->|yes| write_plugin_cache[write_plugin_cache]:::serial --> Done([Compile complete])
  Write -->|no| Done
